<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101955" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχολασ-τικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inclined to ease, enjoying leisure</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ -κώτεραι πόλεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1322b37
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1341a28
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύλλογοι ς</span>.
			<i>lounging</i> parties, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1313b4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ς.</span>
			<i>leisure</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>EN</u>
				1177b22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Astrol.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τόπος</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργός</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				186.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>devoting one's leisure to learning, learned man, scholar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				5.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
				36
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">J.,
				<u>CIG</u>2746</span></i>
				(<span class="entity">Aphrodisias</span>), al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				1921
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>academic, theoretical</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥήτορες</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμπρακτοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.265S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> freq. in bad sense,
				<i>pedant, learned simpleton</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				1.11.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				1.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
				<u>Facet.</u>
				263
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>advocate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phoeb.
				<u>Fig.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; as an officially recognized <i>legal adviser</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				693
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				1.45.2
			</span></i> (V <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMasp.</u>
				2 ii 2
			</span></i>,al. <span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ σχολαστικῶν</span>, =
			<i>ex</i>-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχολαστικός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				5.1701.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>; esp. <i>public advocate</i>,
				Lat.<i>defensor civitatis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IGRom.
				4.765
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Phrygia</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. καὶ ἔκδικος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					1094.1
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
